    {
      "id": 121,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        3040,
        -1560
      ],
      "size": [
        480,
        560
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "title": "FUN CONTROLNET",
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "FUN CONTROLNET — drive the generation with a control video\n\nWorkflow 22's generation pass with the PDD upscale removed, plus\nKijai's curve-form Fun ControlNet Union.\n\nORDER MATTERS. Control applies to the MODEL, before the sigma shift:\n\n    UNETLoader -> H3 Fun ControlNet Apply -> ModelSamplingMiniMaxH3\n                                          -> BasicGuider\n\nThat is the order the pack's own example uses. It patches the model, not\nthe conditioning, so it composes with everything else in the graph.\n\nTHE CONTROL VIDEO IS ALREADY PREPROCESSED. Load a depth, pose, canny,\nHED or MLSD clip -- this graph does not generate one. Frame count should\nmatch the render length, which the Scene Prompt sets.\n\nWEIGHTS: models/controlnet/minimax_h3_fun_controlnet_union_pruned_bf16\n.safetensors. It MUST be the bf16 build. The int8_convrot file is the\nsame network but the pack builds plain Linear modules with no dequant\npath, so it cannot read quantised weights. Your BASE checkpoint stays\nint8 -- the two are independent, and the ControlNet takes its dtype from\nthe hidden states at run time.\n\nFOUR CAVEATS FROM THE AUTHOR, worth reading before blaming the graph:\n  - it was trained against fl2va, and this graph is ref2va\n  - pose holds a figure better than depth, especially when the subject\n    occupies few tokens\n  - only depth and pose are tested; canny, HED and MLSD are unverified\n  - strength above 1.0 degrades rather than controls\n\nTOKEN REORDERING BREAKS CONTROL ALIGNMENT. If you add SLA / Sol-Attn\nstyle attention here, expect the control to stop lining up. Start with\nit out of the graph.\n\nstart_percent / end_percent release control partway down the schedule --\nuseful when structure is set early and you want the tail free."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
